id: pm-1l85at
title: Measure credential_key_assignment false positives against a captured corpus of real agent text instead of review-by-review shapes
description: "pm-gh1704 added the mutation-only credential_key_assignment rule. Its PR 1712 reviews surfaced about a dozen false-positive shapes one round at a time, all fixed and pinned in the secret-policy-parity must-allow corpus: quoted and unquoted prose, masks, placeholders, paths, key-file names, member paths, optional chains, fallback expressions and constant references. The tail is open-ended, and in the default advise mode a false positive costs one warning, while in block mode it refuses a write. Capture a redacted corpus of real pm descriptions, comments and notes (for example from this tracker's history), declare a false-positive-rate measurement over it as an assurance provider, and bound it with an assertion, so new shapes are found by measurement rather than by reviewers."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags[5]: assurance,false-positives,measurement,secret-guard,security
created_at: "2026-11-12T12:19:58.221Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T08:39:03.308Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A redacted corpus of real agent text is committed with capture provenance; An assurance measurement reports the credential_key_assignment false-positive rate over it, and an assertion bounds that rate; Each newly found false positive is added to the corpus with its fix"
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: low
confidence: medium
expected_result: False positives are found by measurement over representative text
actual_result: False positives were found one review round at a time
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-gh1704,discovered_from,"2026-11-12T12:19:58.221Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-17T08:39:03.289Z","harness:claude-code","Scope note from the pm-hw00c2 work (2026-11-17): the tracker itself is a ready corpus of real agent text with capture provenance (git). Parsing every item document with parseItemDocument and scanning title, description, acceptance criteria, close fields, repro and result fields, comments, notes and learnings with scanMutationSecrets gives 47,292 texts across 3,323 items. On the 2026.11.17 build that measured 8 credential_key_assignment and 4 password_assignment hits. Every hit is a synthetic sample quoted in the secret-guard items themselves, so the measured false-positive rate on real prose is zero. Fit with the assurance model: .agents/pm/assurance.json already declares provider measurements (source kind provider, provider repository-quality, one key per receipt). A secret-guard key that reports per-rule finding counts over tracker text, bounded by a ceiling assertion with a negative control, would meet the second criterion without a bespoke gate script. The first criterion (a separate redacted corpus) is then optional, because the tracker text is already committed."
body: ""
